     ee    The next word's first character becomes the escape
          character for cc/CC mode, instead of the default caret.

     hh    Host (server) mode: treat standard input and output as
          the connection to the remote system (no line is opened)
          -- used when kkeerrmmiitt is invoked as a login shell or from
          a getty on a dial-in line.

     tt    Tymnet mode: pause briefly between incoming data pack-
          ets.

     mm    Macintosh mode: send an extra end-of-line character
          after each packet, for MacKermit.

     xx    Leave slashes in file names alone and transmit the
          directory structure (normally only the last component
          of a name is sent).

     aa    Take file names in pairs: the first name of each pair
          is used on the sending side, the second on the
          receiving side.

