NNOOTTEESS
     This is the public-domain Columbia University Kermit for
     UNIX-like systems, ported to COHERENT by Lauren Weinstein
     and Charles Fiterman.

     Without hh, kkeerrmmiitt opens the tty _l_i_n_e itself and assumes it
     is the local end of the connection; with hh it assumes its
     standard input and output are already the remote connection.
